From: LukeOkk <85941941+LukeOkk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:14:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] interpreter: use the switch interpreter with a heap
 reference base (SteamARM, HYPOTHESIS)

HYPOTHESIS, UNTESTED: not compiled, not run.

The arm64 assembly interpreter (mterp) loads a dex register with GET_VREG
into a W register and uses the X register as a base address (iget/iput
fast paths, array-length, aget/aput) or passes it to C++ helpers as a
mirror::Object* (artIGetObjectFromMterp, artAGetObjectFromMterp,
artLockObjectFromCode, MterpFillArrayData, ...); throw stores it into
Thread::exception_ and return-object hands it back as a JValue. Each would
need the base ORed in (SteamARM counts about 20 sites).

Until that port exists, CanUseMterp() is false when the base is non-zero:
every thread runs the switch interpreter, which reads and writes dex
registers through StackReference and so follows the central compression.
Building with ART_USE_CXX_INTERPRETER=true removes mterp altogether.
arm64 has no nterp in Android 11 (nterp_stub.cc).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L6ANQQienC2qRCeZBzUfuS
---
 runtime/interpreter/mterp/mterp.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runtime/interpreter/mterp/mterp.cc b/runtime/interpreter/mterp/mterp.cc
index c6d3258..d5d6177 100644
--- a/runtime/interpreter/mterp/mterp.cc
+++ b/runtime/interpreter/mterp/mterp.cc
@@ -147,6 +147,12 @@ bool CanUseMterp()
     REQUIRES_SHARED(Locks::mutator_lock_) {
   const Runtime* const runtime = Runtime::Current();
   return
+      // SteamARM (HYPOTHESIS): the arm64 assembly interpreter dereferences
+      // 32-bit dex register values directly and passes them to C++ helpers as
+      // pointers (runtime/interpreter/mterp/arm64/*.S, about 20 sites). It is
+      // not ported to a heap reference base; the switch interpreter (C++,
+      // through the typed references) runs instead.
+      kHeapReferenceBase == 0u &&
       runtime->IsStarted() &&
       !runtime->IsAotCompiler() &&
       !runtime->GetInstrumentation()->IsActive() &&
